{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1430","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1430","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1430\",\"parent_revision\":\"9a5faf4c9f2348590c80d9b49d2bd06bec4a32d3\",\"root_revision\":\"81b60eab02f22ab4dbf21fa917c15c20bf248743bfa05a64724ac97516ad7292\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Current state\\n\\nThe `swarm-patterns` skill (Pattern 1 -- Parallel Specialists) dispatches multiple review agents in parallel, but agents return unstructured findings as free-text messages via `SendMessage`. There is no mechanism to:\\n\\n1. Assign confidence scores to individual findings (e.g., \\\"high confidence: SQL injection in auth.py line 42\\\" vs \\\"low confidence: possible performance issue\\\")\\n2. Deduplicate findings when multiple review agents flag the same issue from different perspectives\\n3. Gate whether a finding is surfaced to the user based on a confidence threshold\\n\\nThe `code-review` agent (`.claude/agents/code-review.md`) produces categorized output (critical/warning) but has no structured confidence scoring schema. When multiple review agents run in parallel (as in the swarm-patterns parallel specialists recipe), duplicate findings accumulate without consolidation.\\n\\nIssue #1423 tracks persona-based specialized review agents but does NOT address confidence scoring or deduplication -- it focuses on splitting the single code-reviewer into domain-specific agents. This issue is complementary: #1423 creates the specialized agents, this issue ensures their output is consolidated and filtered.\\n\\n### Target state\\n\\nThe `swarm-patterns` skill's \\\"Pattern 1 -- Parallel Specialists\\\" recipe includes a post-collection consolidation step. Review agents emit structured findings with a confidence field (e.g., `confidence: high | medium | low`). The orchestrator applies two post-processing steps before presenting results:\\n\\n1. **Dedup**: Findings from different agents referencing the same file + line range + issue category are merged into a single finding, noting which agents flagged it\\n2. **Confidence gate**: Findings below a configurable threshold (default: medium) are grouped into a \\\"Low confidence -- verify manually\\\" section rather than presented as blocking issues\\n\\nThe consolidation logic lives in a reference file (e.g., `swarm-patterns/references/review-consolidation.md`) that teaches the orchestrator how to merge and filter findings.\\n\\n### Measurable signal\\n\\nThe `swarm-patterns` SKILL.md Pattern 1 recipe includes a \\\"Consolidate findings\\\" step between \\\"Wait for results\\\" and \\\"Synthesize findings and cleanup\\\". A reference file `references/review-consolidation.md` exists in the swarm-patterns skill directory. The reference file defines the structured finding schema (file, line range, category, confidence, description) and the dedup/gating algorithm.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Confidence gating and deduplication pipeline for multi-agent review findings\\nDate: 2026-04-03\\nGoal: Add structured confidence scoring, deduplication, and confidence-threshold gating to swarm-patterns Pattern 1 parallel specialist recipe.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. swarm-patterns SKILL.md exists and Pattern 1 recipe is defined | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read .claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md lines 17-53\\n2. code-review agent exists and output format known | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read .claude/agents/code-review.md lines 152-197\\n3. No consolidation step in Pattern 1 | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: swarm-patterns/SKILL.md lines 44-52 confirmed\\n4. No swarm-patterns/references/ dir | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Glob returned no files\\n5. review-consolidation.md does not exist | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Glob confirmed absence\\n6. Structured finding schema derivable | Snapshot: DERIVABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: compound-engineering-plugin.md lines 134-138 documents exact schema; code-review.md output format known -- schema fully specifiable\\n7. Dedup algorithm design | Snapshot: DERIVABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Issue description specifies \\\"same file + line range + issue category\\\" merge criteria; confirmed by compound-engineering prior art\\n8. Confidence gating config mechanism | Snapshot: DERIVABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Issue specifies default=medium; \\\"configurable threshold\\\" = orchestrator-instruction-based (inline reference file), no runtime code needed\\n9. #1423 dependency state | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: gh issue view 1423 = OPEN, complementary not blocking\\n10. compound-engineering reference implementation | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: research/skill-generation-tools/compound-engineering-plugin.md confirmed\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE -> AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker -- compound-engineering schema documented, code-review output format confirmed)\\n- Condition 7: DERIVABLE -> AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker -- issue description specifies exact merge criteria)\\n- Condition 8: DERIVABLE -> AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker -- no runtime config needed, inline reference instruction sufficient)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **confidence gating and deduplication for multi-agent review findings** so that **parallel review agents produce consolidated, high-signal output instead of duplicated and unfiltered findings**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/compound-engineering-plugin.md -- pattern: Parallel agent dispatch with confidence scoring and deduplication pipelines\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-03)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Observable gap** (confirmed):\\n\\n1. Load `swarm-patterns` skill\\n2. Follow Pattern 1 (Parallel Specialists) with 2+ review agents\\n3. Observe: agents return free-text messages via SendMessage with no confidence field\\n4. Observe: no consolidation step between \\\"Wait for results\\\" and \\\"Synthesize findings and cleanup\\\"\\n5. If two agents flag the same issue, they appear as separate findings with no merge\\n\\n**Success signal** (from item description):\\n\\n- `swarm-patterns` SKILL.md Pattern 1 recipe includes a \\\"Consolidate findings\\\" step between \\\"Wait for results\\\" and \\\"Synthesize findings and cleanup\\\"\\n- A file `swarm-patterns/references/review-consolidation.md` exists\\n- The reference file defines: structured finding schema (file, line range, category, confidence, description) + dedup algorithm (same file + line range + category = merge) + confidence gate (default: medium, configurable)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1 \u2014 High\\n\\n**Rationale**: The swarm-patterns skill's Pattern 1 is the primary multi-agent code review recipe in this repository. Without confidence gating and deduplication, parallel specialist reviews produce noisy, duplicated output that degrades trust in the review system. This directly undermines the value of #1423 (persona-based review agents, also P1). The fix is purely additive (new reference file + one step in Pattern 1) with no breaking changes.\\n\\n**Dependency on #1423**: Independent. Both can ship in either order. Shipping this item first improves any existing parallel review setup. Shipping #1423 first creates the specialized agents that will benefit most from this consolidation pipeline.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Scope**: Additive documentation change \u2014 no runtime code, no breaking changes.\\n\\n**Files changed**:\\n- `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` \u2014 Pattern 1 and Workflow 1 updated (add one step, replace placeholder comment)\\n- `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/references/review-consolidation.md` \u2014 New file created\\n\\n**Secondary file** (optional, recommended):\\n- `.claude/agents/code-review.md` \u2014 Add confidence field to output template\\n\\n**Users affected**: Anyone using swarm-patterns Pattern 1 for parallel code review. Change is backward-compatible \u2014 existing reviews continue to work; confidence field is opt-in via the reference file instructions.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` Pattern 1 recipe includes a \\\"Consolidate findings\\\" step between step 3 (Wait for results) and step 4 (Synthesize findings and cleanup)\\n- [ ] The \\\"Consolidate findings\\\" step references `references/review-consolidation.md`\\n- [ ] `swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` Workflow 1 comment at lines 339-340 is replaced with a reference to the \\\"Consolidate findings\\\" step\\n- [ ] File `swarm-patterns/references/review-consolidation.md` is created\\n- [ ] `review-consolidation.md` defines the structured finding schema: file, line range, category, confidence (high/medium/low), description, agents (list of which agents flagged it)\\n- [ ] `review-consolidation.md` defines the dedup algorithm: findings with same file + overlapping line range + same category are merged into one finding with combined agents list\\n- [ ] `review-consolidation.md` defines the confidence gate: findings below configurable threshold (default: medium) are grouped into a separate \\\"Low confidence -- verify manually\\\" section\\n- [ ] `review-consolidation.md` includes an example showing the consolidation output format\\n- [ ] (Recommended) `code-review.md` output template includes a confidence field\\n- [ ] Both SKILL.md and review-consolidation.md pass `uv run prek run --files <file>`\\n\\n### Research\\n\\n**Reference implementation**: compound-engineering /ce:review skill\\n- Source: research/skill-generation-tools/compound-engineering-plugin.md lines 134-138\\n- Key insight: \\\"Confidence gating: Suppresses false positives, requires high confidence for blocking issues\\\" and \\\"Dedup pipeline: Consolidates duplicate findings across agent instances\\\"\\n- Schema pattern: structured JSON with confidence scores per finding\\n\\n**Prior research insight**:\\n- Source: research/insights/2026-04-03-compound-engineering-plugin-improvements.md\\n- Contains: exact current state, target state, and measurable signal description\\n- Gap confirmed: synthesis placeholder at swarm-patterns/SKILL.md lines 339-340 has no documented pattern\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md\\n.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/references/review-consolidation.md\\n.claude/agents/code-review.md (recommended update)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Required**:\\n- None. This item is purely additive.\\n\\n**Complementary** (not blocking):\\n- Issue #1423 (Persona-based specialized review agents for quality gates) \u2014 creates specialized agents that will use this consolidation pipeline. Can ship independently in any order.\\n\\n**Reference implementation**:\\n- research/skill-generation-tools/compound-engineering-plugin.md \u2014 documents compound-engineering /ce:review confidence gating and dedup pipeline (prior art)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Effort**: Small\\n\\n- 1 new file (review-consolidation.md, ~100-150 lines): finding schema, dedup algorithm, confidence gate algorithm, example output\\n- 1 existing file updated (swarm-patterns/SKILL.md): add one step to Pattern 1 recipe and update Workflow 1 comment\\n- 1 optional file update (code-review.md): add confidence field to output template\\n- No runtime code changes\\n- No migration needed\\n\\n**Estimated**: 1-2 hours for documentation authoring + linting pass\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\nThe system dispatches parallel review agents and collects results via SendMessage but lacks a post-collection quality filter. Findings accumulate without deduplication or confidence filtering before being presented to the user. This is a structural gap in an existing workflow -- the pipeline runs correctly but the output is unfiltered.\\n\\n**Root-Cause Analysis**: Not applicable (not a defect or recurring-pattern type)\\n\\n**Complementary item**: #1423 (Persona-based specialized review agents) creates the specialized agents; this item ensures their output is consolidated and filtered. Both must ship for the full review pipeline to be high-signal. Neither blocks the other -- they can be worked independently.\\n\\n## Agent Instructions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- None identified. The consolidation logic lives in a reference file (skill-level documentation), not an agent instruction file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Working Directory\\n/home/user/claude_skills\\n\\n### Branch\\nclaude/automate-backlog-processing-H5FfF\\n\\n### Primary Deliverable Files\\n- .claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md (edit -- Pattern 1 + Workflow 1 only)\\n- .claude/skills/swarm-patterns/references/review-consolidation.md (new file)\\n- .claude/skills/swarm-patterns/examples/review-consolidation-example.md (new file, optional)\\n\\n### Plan Artifacts\\n- plan/P1430-confidence-gating-deduplication.yaml (task plan, 3 tasks)\\n- plan/architect-confidence-gating-deduplication.md (architecture spec)\\n- plan/feature-context-confidence-gating-and-deduplication-pipeline-for-multi-agent-review-findings.md (feature context)\\n- plan/codebase/patterns.md, plan/codebase/architecture.md, plan/codebase/testing.md\\n\\